Below is the last answer from WEX lawyer. I think the last proposition is ok. If We can handle the communications under this clause iwthout any issue. Of course, I’ll let leave the final comment on it.

{color:#0747a6}Good morning,{color}

{color:#0747a6}I spoke with Katie Rushton yesterday about this contract and the outstanding points we had discussed with Ishmael. This is the progress I have made:{color}

# {color:#0747a6}Supplier Code of Conduct.{color}

{color:#0747a6}The Code used by Bolt duplicates provisions that WEX already has in place. Accordingly, we will accept the wording in clause 6.1 of the agreement that refers to it and obliges WEX to comply with the Supplier Code of Conduct.{color}

# {color:#0747a6}Use of WEX marks.{color}

{color:#0747a6}The wording that I had proposed for this clause is WEX's standard wording for a reseller agreement. This is the wording I had proposed:{color}

{color:#0747a6}WEX grants Bolt a non-exclusive, revocable and limited license to display and use the WEX Trade Marks during the term of this Agreement only in the manner prescribed or permitted by WEX from time to time in connection with this Agreement. In exercising the license granted under this Clause, Bolt undertakes that it shall not use the  WEX Trade Marks  in any manner which, in the reasonable opinion of WEX, may diminish WEX’ reputation. {color}



{color:#0747a6}Bolt are insisting on their own wording but that offers no protection to WEX that Bolt will use our marks responsibly. The simple solution would seem to be to merge the two wordings as follows:{color}



{color:#0747a6}_Partner grants Bolt a non-exclusive, non-transferable, royalty-free license (with the right to sub-license to Bolt group companies) to use Partner's trademarks and copyrighted works to:_{color}

* {color:#0747a6}_promote, advertise and display the Driver Partnership Offers on Bolt Platform/App and any other communication channel;_{color}
* {color:#0747a6}_prepare presentations, press releases and case studies to share with third parties to promote the Driver Partnership Offerings generally;_{color}

{color:#0747a6}_provided that Bolt shall not use the Partner's trademarks in any manner which in the reasonable opinion of Partner (WEX) may diminish WEX' reputation._{color}



{color:#0747a6}The above suggested wording would allow Bolt to promote offers as they wish while offering WEX the protection we require.{color}



{color:#0747a6}Feel free to copy this email to Bolt. I wonder if it would be possible for me to meet with Bolt's lawyer to see if we can agree this final point?{color}

