Hey [~accountid:6151cf6878e5e40070fb74c2] here are the answers to your questions:

Clause 1.3.  The definition of the Cancellation Fee should also include the fee charged to the Client by the Driver for delivering an Excluded Package under Clause 2.6.

Question: Does it mean that if the Driver delivers an Excluded Package to the Recipient, we will charge the Client the cancellation fee? Is this a regulatory requirement?
{color:#ff5630}LP:  No.  The Cancellation Fee will be charged to the Client only when the Driver cancels the delivery because the Client sent the Excluded Packages or unsuitable packages under Clause 2.6 of the T&Cs.  This requirement has already existed in Clause 2.6 of the T&Cs before we reviewed it.  This is not a regulatory requirement but we recommend revising Clause 1.3 to be in line with Clause 2.6{color}

{color:#ff5630}We have made further revision to Clause 1.3 of the T&Cs to make it clear as attached.{color}

Clause 2.6.  To comply with Clause 3(1) of the Guidelines, we recommend adding this wording: “In the event that the Diver and/or Bolt have reasonable grounds to suspect or believe that the Package contains illegal items, illegal substances, and/or narcotics, the Driver and/or Bolt shall have the right to inform the Royal Thai Police or the Office of the Narcotics Control Board immediately”.

Question: We are not against adding this clause to the T&Cs but just curious - don’t Driver and Bolt have this right by default under the law or it needs to be expressly prescribed in the T&Cs?
{color:#ff5630}LP:  The Driver and Bolt have this reporting duty by default under the law.  However, we recommend specifying this duty in the T&Cs to ensure that all relevant parties know about this and fully comply with it.{color}

Clause 2.8.  Bolt should provide management plans for accidents or emergencies to reduce loss or damage to the Driver under Clause 3(2) of the Guidelines.

Question: Could you please clarify what this means in practice? Do we need to set up certain guidelines/processes for our Operations Team for this purpose?
{color:#ff5630}LP: The Guidelines of the DLT did not provide the criteria and/or scope of the management plans.  According to the Guidelines, Bolt should set up the management plans for accidents or emergency events that sufficiently cover the details, e.g. when an incident is considered an accident or an emergency event, guidelines for prevention of such accident or emergency event, how to handle them, etc., to reduce loss or damage to the Drivers as Bolt finds appropriate.{color}



